      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To determine the incidence and risk factors for delirium after coronary artery bypass graft (CABG) surgery."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "Prospective cohort."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "Cardiac surgery units of a tertiary care hospital."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PARTICIPANTS",
          "content": "Consecutive patients over age 65 years undergoing elective CABG surgery. Exclusion criteria included preoperative sensory or language barriers."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INTERVENTIONS",
          "content": "Each patient was assessed within 24 h before surgery for baseline demographic, medical and functional data. Incident delirium (within four postoperative days) was diagnosed by a study physician. Nine potential risk factors for delirium were subjected to univariate and multivariate analysis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "MAIN RESULTS",
          "content": "Of 75 consenting patients, three died during or soon after surgery and one was still comatose at follow-up. Of the remaining 71 participants, 23 (32%) experienced delirium. Those with delirium were more likely than those without delirium to have a history of a stroke (21% versus 4%, respectively, P=0.032) and to have had a longer duration of cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB) (113 mins versus 95 mins, respectively, P=0.025). A tendency to have experienced low cardiac output (83% versus 58%, respectively, P=0.061) postoperatively was also noted. Multivariate analysis confirmed past stroke and duration of cardiopulmonary bypass as risk factors."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Delirium in the elderly after CABG surgery is common. Its occurrence may be predisposed by a history of a stroke and precipitated by a longer duration of CPB."
        }
      ]},
